// End-to-end browser smoke test for the Gold Box asset viewer.
//
// Boots the Vite dev server (needed for /@fs access to the real game files),
// drives headless Edge via puppeteer-core, and asserts that every bundled game
// and a representative asset from each container format actually decodes and
// renders, with no fatal console errors. Exits non-zero on any failure.
//
//   npm run e2e
//
// Requires the local game data (the repo game folders + amiga_extracted/). When a data-dependent
// case's own assets are not being served, that case reports SKIP instead of FAIL — but ONLY the
// cases that opt in, by naming `dataAbsent` in their own `pass` expression — 55 of the ~150 cases
// do so today; the table-driven `runCase` entries and the rest of the bespoke cases do NOT. A case
// without that disjunct still FAILs when its data is missing, deliberately:
// the exemption is opt-in per case, not a blanket suite-wide amnesty.
// Separately, a whole-suite run in which all four `kind: 'game'` cases render 0 frames takes the
// explicit fresh-clone branch at the bottom of main(), which prints only the data-INDEPENDENT
// cases and can therefore exit 0 on a clone with no game data at all.
// See `dataAbsent` below for what "not being served" actually looks like on the dev server — it is
// NOT a 404.

